/-!
# The top cohomology of the dual Koszul tower is the tower of quotients by the generators

Let `Y` be a scheme, let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪_Y` and let `ℱ` be a sheaf of
`𝒪_Y`-modules. The dual Koszul tower `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulDualSystemOn` is the
inverse system of the complexes `K(𝒪_Y, f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1}) ⊗ ℱ`, concentrated in the degrees
`0, …, r`. This file identifies **its tower of top cohomology sheaves with the tower of quotients
of `ℱ` by the subsheaves generated by the powers of the generators**,

`H^r(K(𝒪_Y, f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1}) ⊗ ℱ)  ≅  ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`,  naturally in `n`,

where the right-hand side is `Stacks.Algebraization.globalSpanMultiple` at the exponent `n + 1`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulGlobalGenerator` — the chosen global sections of `𝒪_Y`, read in
  `Γ(Y, ⊤)`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulTopQuotientSystem` — the tower
  `n ↦ ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`, as a `Stacks.Algebraization.submoduleQuotientSystem`, and
  `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulQuotientπ` its projections.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulDualTowerOn` — the dual Koszul tower, read in `Y.Modules`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulTopSingleComparison` and
  `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulDualToTopQuotient` — the comparison at one level and as a morphism
  of towers.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.koszulGenMap_comp_cokernel_π_globalSpanMultiple` — the generator map is
  killed by the projection onto `ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`. This is the affine-local
  direction: a section `f_i^{n+1} · x` over an arbitrary open restricts, on every affine open,
  into the generators of the subsheaf, and membership in a submodule of a sheaf of modules is
  affine-local.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.globalSpanMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule_koszulGenMap` — the converse: the
  subsheaf is killed by the projection onto the cokernel of the generator map. Here the
  affine-local universal property of the subsheaf is what is used, and a general element of the
  generated ideal is expanded by `Ideal.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient` — **the top cohomology sheaf of the
  Koszul complex is the quotient**, at one level.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_homologyMap_koszulTopSingleComparison` — **the comparison of towers
  is an isomorphism on cohomology in the top degree, at every level**, which is the hypothesis of
  [Stacks, Tag 0G3D] there.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.homologyIsoCokernelKoszulGeneratorsMap` identifies the top
cohomology sheaf with the cokernel of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulGeneratorsMap`, the map
`ℱ^r ⟶ ℱ` given by `(x_i) ↦ ∑_i f_i^{n+1} x_i`. Two things separate that from the quotient tower
the adic comparison of `Completion/GlobalSpanAdicProIso.lean` is about:

* the cokernel of a morphism is not a quotient by a *subsheaf*. The subsheaf
  `globalSpanMultiple` is cut out affine-locally — it is the least subsheaf containing
  `(f_i^{n+1}|_U) · Γ(ℱ, U)` on every affine open — and identifying it with the image of
  `koszulGeneratorsMap` is an affine-local argument in both directions, carried out below;
* the Koszul level `n` uses the exponent `n + 1`, so the comparison is with the quotient tower
  **reindexed**, `n ↦ ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`.

The identification is moreover needed *naturally in `n`*, which
`homologyIsoCokernelKoszulGeneratorsMap` does not provide. Naturality is obtained here by
characterising the comparison through `HomologicalComplex.topToHomology`: in the top degree the
cohomology object is a cokernel of the incoming differential with `topToHomology` as its
projection (`HomologicalComplex.isColimitCokernelCoforkTopToHomology`), so every identification
of it is pinned down by one equation, and the transition maps are compared by the universal
property rather than by unfolding a chain of isomorphisms.

The Koszul constructions are stated on the small Zariski site
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf`, whose sheaf of rings and `Y.ringCatSheaf` are
definitionally but not reducibly equal. A goal mixing the two spellings is not type-correct at the
transparency `rw` matches at, and the symptom is a rewrite failing on a pattern that is plainly
present. Every Koszul datum used below is therefore **ascribed once** into the scheme's own
presentation — `koszulComplexOn`, `koszulGenMap`, `koszulGenSingle`, `koszulGenMul`,
`koszulTopProjOn`, `koszulToCoIdx`, `koszulFromCoIdx`, `koszulDualTowerOn`, `koszulDualMapOn` —
and nothing below mentions the site again except through those. For the same reason
`koszulQuotientπ` exists: a term `cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) N.ι` has a submodule of the other
presentation inside it, and goals containing it are not reducibly type-correct either.

The degree is written `r - 1 + 1` throughout, as in `KoszulTopCohomologySheaf.lean`, so that the
top projection and the two reindexings of that file apply on the nose; `(r : ℤ) - 1 + 1` and
`(r : ℤ)` are equal but not definitionally equal, and `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.Idx` at the
two spellings are different types.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0913](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0913)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech

universe u

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.submoduleCompleteLattice

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

/-! ## The generators as global sections of the structure sheaf -/

section Scheme

open scoped IsMulCommutative

attribute [local instance]
  sectionsModuleΓ sectionsModuleΓSheaf sectionsModuleRingCatSheaf sectionsSMulCommClassΓ
  monoSubmoduleι

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections
    ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  (ℱ : Y.Modules)

/-- **Multiplication by `f_i^{n+1}` on `ℱ`, read in `Y.Modules`.** The construction is on the
small Zariski site of `Y`; this ascribes its type in the scheme's own presentation of the
category of modules, so that the submodules and quotients below, which are stated there, compose
with it without a transport. -/
def koszulGenMul (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r) : ℱ ⟶ ℱ :=
  RingedSite.koszulScalarOn (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f
    (RingedSite.koszulGenExp n i) ℱ

/-- **The chosen global sections of `𝒪_Y`**, read in `Γ(Y, ⊤)`: the ringed-site datum
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal` evaluated at the terminal open. -/
def koszulGlobalGenerator (i : Fin r) : Γ(Y, ⊤) :=
  globalSectionOver Y (f i) ⊤

/-- Restricting the `i`-th generator from `Γ(Y, ⊤)` to an affine open is its value there. -/
theorem globalRes_koszulGlobalGenerator (U : Y.affineOpens) (i : Fin r) :
    globalRes U (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f i) = globalSectionOver Y (f i) U.1 :=
  RingedSite.globalSectionVal_map (f i) (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.1))).op

/-- The value over an affine open of the monomial of the `i`-th generator is the `(n+1)`-st power
of the restriction of that generator. -/
theorem koszulValueOver_eq_globalRes_pow (U : Y.affineOpens) (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r) :
    koszulValueOver Y f (RingedSite.koszulGenExp n i) U.1 =
      globalRes U (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f i) ^ (n + 1) :=
  (koszulValueOver_koszulGenExp Y f n U.1 i).trans
    (congrArg (fun c => c ^ (n + 1)) (globalRes_koszulGlobalGenerator Y f U i).symm)

/-- The `(n+1)`-st power of the restriction of the `i`-th generator is one of the generators of
the affine-local ideal `Stacks.Algebraization.globalSpanIdeals`. -/
theorem globalRes_pow_mem_globalSpanIdeals (U : Y.affineOpens) (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r) :
    globalRes U (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f i) ^ (n + 1) ∈
      globalSpanIdeals (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) U :=
  Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-! ## The quotient tower -/

/-- **The tower `n ↦ ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`**, the quotient tower of the subsheaves
generated by the powers of the generators, indexed so that level `n` carries the exponent
`n + 1` — which is the exponent the Koszul level `n` uses. -/
def koszulTopQuotientSystem : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ Y.Modules :=
  submoduleQuotientSystem ℱ (fun n => globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ)
    (fun _ _ h => globalSpanMultiple_antitone (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) ℱ
      (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1))

/-- The quotient projection `ℱ ⟶ ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ` onto level `n` of the
tower.

Its type mentions neither a cokernel nor a submodule, which is what keeps the goals below
type-correct at the transparency `rw` matches at. -/
def koszulQuotientπ (n : ℕ) : ℱ ⟶ (koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).obj (op n) :=
  cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ).ι

/-- The quotient projection `ℱ ⟶ ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ` is an epimorphism. -/
instance epi_koszulQuotientπ (n : ℕ) : Epi (koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n) :=
  coequalizer.π_epi

/-- The projections are compatible with the transition maps of the tower. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem koszulQuotientπ_comp_map {m n : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) :
    koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ m ≫ (koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).map (homOfLE h).op =
      koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n :=
  quotientMapOfLE_π (globalSpanMultiple_antitone (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) ℱ
    (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1))

/-! ## The generator map and the subsheaf generated by the powers of the generators -/

/-- Over an affine open, multiplication by `f_i^{n+1}` acts on sections as the `(n+1)`-st power
of the restricted generator. -/
private theorem koszulGenMul_app_apply (U : Y.affineOpens) (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r)
    (x : ℱ.val.obj (op U.1)) :
    ((koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i).val.app (op U.1)).hom x =
      globalRes U (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f i) ^ (n + 1) • x :=
  (RingedSite.koszulScalarOn_app (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f
      (RingedSite.koszulGenExp n i) ℱ (op U.1) x).trans
    (congrArg (fun c : Γ(Y, U.1) => c • x) (koszulValueOver_eq_globalRes_pow Y f U n i))

/-- **Multiplication by `f_i^{n+1}` carries a section over an arbitrary open into the subsheaf
`(f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`.**

The subsheaf is cut out affine-locally, so this is proved affine-locally: membership in a
submodule of a sheaf of modules is a local condition
(`Stacks.Algebraization.mem_submodule_of_affine`), and over an affine open the section
`f_i^{n+1} · x` is one of the generators of the defining ideal acting on a section. -/
theorem koszulGenMul_app_mem_globalSpanMultiple (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r)
    (U : Y.Opens) (x : Γ(ℱ, U)) :
    ((koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i).val.app (op U)).hom x ∈
      (globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ).toSubmodule.obj (op U) := by
  refine mem_submodule_of_affine _ U _ fun V ι => ?_
  have hnat : (show ℱ.val.obj (op V.1) from (ℱ.val.map ι.op).hom
        (((koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i).val.app (op U)).hom x)) =
      globalRes V (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f i) ^ (n + 1) •
        (show ℱ.val.obj (op V.1) from (ℱ.val.map ι.op).hom x) :=
    (congrArg (fun k => k x)
        (PresheafOfModules.Hom.naturality (koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i).val ι.op)).symm.trans
      (koszulGenMul_app_apply Y f ℱ V n i _)
  exact Eq.mpr
    (congrArg (· ∈ (globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ).toSubmodule.obj
      (op V.1)) hnat)
    ((affineLocalMultiple_le_iff (globalSpanIdeals (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1)) ℱ _).1
      le_rfl V
      (Submodule.smul_mem_smul (globalRes_pow_mem_globalSpanIdeals Y f V n i)
        (Submodule.mem_top (x := (show ℱ.val.obj (op V.1) from (ℱ.val.map ι.op).hom x)))))

/-! ## The Koszul data, read in the scheme's own presentation of its modules -/

/-- The Koszul complex with coefficients in `ℱ`, read in `Y.Modules`. -/
def koszulComplexOn (n : ℕ) : CochainComplex Y.Modules ℤ :=
  RingedSite.koszulPowerComplexOn (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ n

/-- The generator map `ℱ^r ⟶ ℱ`, `(x_i) ↦ ∑_i f_i^{n+1} x_i`, read in `Y.Modules`. -/
def koszulGenMap (n : ℕ) : (∏ᶜ fun _ : Fin r => ℱ) ⟶ ℱ :=
  RingedSite.koszulGeneratorsMap (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f n ℱ

/-- The inclusion of the `i`-th factor of `ℱ^r`, read in `Y.Modules`. -/
def koszulGenSingle (i : Fin r) : ℱ ⟶ (∏ᶜ fun _ : Fin r => ℱ) :=
  koszulSingle (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) ℱ i

/-- Multiplication by `f_i^{n+1}` is the `i`-th inclusion followed by the generator map. -/
theorem koszulGenSingle_comp_koszulGenMap (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r) :
    koszulGenSingle Y ℱ i ≫ koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n = koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i :=
  koszulSingle_comp_koszulGeneratorsMap (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f n ℱ i

/-- **Multiplication by `f_i^{n+1}` is killed by the projection onto the cokernel of the generator
map**, being a factor of it. -/
theorem koszulGenMul_comp_cokernel_π (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r) :
    koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i ≫ cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n) = 0 := by
  rw [← koszulGenSingle_comp_koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n i, Category.assoc,
    cokernel.condition (C := Y.Modules), comp_zero]

/-- **The subsheaf `(f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ` is killed by the projection onto the cokernel of
the generator map.**

This is the direction in which the affine-local *universal property* of the subsheaf is used: it
suffices to check the containment on affine opens, where the subsheaf is cut out by
`(f_i^{n+1}|_U) · Γ(ℱ, U)`, and each of those sections is in the image of the generator map by
`Stacks.Algebraization.koszulGenMul_comp_cokernel_π`. A general element of the ideal is expanded
by `Ideal.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun`. -/
theorem globalSpanMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule_koszulGenMap (n : ℕ) :
    globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ ≤
      kernelSubmodule (cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n)) := by
  refine (affineLocalMultiple_le_iff (globalSpanIdeals (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1)) ℱ
    _).2 fun U => Submodule.smul_le.2 fun c hc x _ => ?_
  rw [kernelSubmodule_toSubmodule_obj]
  have hgen : ∀ j : Fin r,
      globalRes U (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f j) ^ (n + 1) •
          (show ℱ.val.obj (op U.1) from x) ∈
        LinearMap.ker ((cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules)
          (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n)).val.app (op U.1)).hom := by
    intro j
    have happ := koszulGenMul_app_apply Y f ℱ U n j x
    have hzero : ((cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n)).val.app (op U.1)).hom
        (((koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n j).val.app (op U.1)).hom x) = 0 :=
      congrArg (fun k : ℱ ⟶ cokernel (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n) =>
        (k.val.app (op U.1)).hom x) (koszulGenMul_comp_cokernel_π Y f ℱ n j)
    exact LinearMap.mem_ker.2 (Eq.mp (congrArg (fun y =>
      ((cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n)).val.app (op U.1)).hom y = 0)
        happ) hzero)
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun.1 hc
  rw [← hd, Finset.sum_smul]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => ?_
  rw [mul_smul]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hgen j)

/-- **Multiplication by `f_i^{n+1}` is killed by the projection onto
`ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`**: its image lies in the subsheaf quotiented out, which is the
sectionwise kernel of the projection. -/
theorem koszulGenMul_comp_cokernel_π_globalSpanMultiple (n : ℕ) (i : Fin r) :
    koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i ≫ koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n = 0 := by
  refine Scheme.Modules.hom_ext _ _ fun V => ?_
  ext x
  have hmem := koszulGenMul_app_mem_globalSpanMultiple Y f ℱ n i V x
  rw [← kernelSubmodule_cokernel_π
    (globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ),
    kernelSubmodule_toSubmodule_obj] at hmem
  exact hmem

/-- The generator map is the sum, over the generators, of a projection followed by multiplication
by that generator. -/
theorem koszulGenMap_eq_sum (n : ℕ) :
    koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n =
      ∑ i : Fin r, Pi.π (fun _ : Fin r => ℱ) i ≫ koszulGenMul Y f ℱ n i :=
  rfl

/-- **The generator map `ℱ^r ⟶ ℱ` is killed by the projection onto
`ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`.** -/
theorem koszulGenMap_comp_cokernel_π_globalSpanMultiple (n : ℕ) :
    koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n ≫ koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n = 0 := by
  rw [koszulGenMap_eq_sum, Preadditive.sum_comp]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i _ => ?_
  rw [Category.assoc, koszulGenMul_comp_cokernel_π_globalSpanMultiple, comp_zero]

/-! ## The top cohomology sheaf is the quotient -/

/-- The degree above the top degree. -/
theorem next_top_eq_succ : (ComplexShape.up ℤ).next ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) = (r : ℤ) - 1 + 1 + 1 :=
  ComplexShape.next_eq' _ rfl

/-- The degree below the top degree. -/
theorem prev_top_eq_pred : (ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) = (r : ℤ) - 1 :=
  (ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev_eq' rfl

/-- The differential out of the top degree of the Koszul complex vanishes. -/
theorem koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).d ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1 + 1) = 0 :=
  RingedSite.koszulPowerComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero'
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f n ℱ

/-- The top-degree term of the Koszul complex, projected onto its unique factor `ℱ`. -/
def koszulTopProjOn (n : ℕ) : (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).X ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ⟶ ℱ :=
  RingedSite.koszulTopProj (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) r ℱ

/-- The projection of the top-degree term of the Koszul complex onto `ℱ` is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_koszulTopProjOn (n : ℕ) : IsIso (koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n) :=
  RingedSite.isIso_koszulTopProj (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) r ℱ

/-- The last differential of the Koszul complex, read into `ℱ` through the top projection, is the
top differential of `KoszulTopCohomologySheaf.lean`. -/
theorem d_comp_koszulTopProjOn (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).d ((r : ℤ) - 1) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ≫ koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n =
      RingedSite.koszulTopDifferential (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f n ℱ :=
  congrArg (fun φ => φ ≫ koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n)
    (AlternatingCech.complex_d
      (RingedSite.koszulPowerFunctorOn (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ n)
      ((r : ℤ) - 1))

/-- The sign-weighted reindexing from `ℱ^r` to the term of the Koszul complex below the top
degree, read in `Y.Modules`. -/
def koszulToCoIdx (n : ℕ) :
    (∏ᶜ fun _ : Fin r => ℱ) ⟶ (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).X ((r : ℤ) - 1) :=
  RingedSite.toCoIdxProduct (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) r ℱ

/-- The sign-weighted reindexing in the other direction, read in `Y.Modules`. -/
def koszulFromCoIdx (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).X ((r : ℤ) - 1) ⟶ (∏ᶜ fun _ : Fin r => ℱ) :=
  RingedSite.fromCoIdxProduct (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) r ℱ

/-- **The last differential of the Koszul complex factors through the generator map.** -/
theorem koszulFromCoIdx_comp_koszulGenMap (n : ℕ) :
    koszulFromCoIdx Y f ℱ n ≫ koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n =
      (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).d ((r : ℤ) - 1) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ≫ koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n :=
  (RingedSite.koszulTopDifferential_comp_eq
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f n ℱ).trans
      (d_comp_koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n).symm

/-- **The generator map factors through the last differential of the Koszul complex.** -/
theorem koszulToCoIdx_comp_d_comp_koszulTopProjOn (n : ℕ) :
    koszulToCoIdx Y f ℱ n ≫
        ((koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).d ((r : ℤ) - 1) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ≫
          koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n) =
      koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n :=
  (congrArg (fun φ => koszulToCoIdx Y f ℱ n ≫ φ) (d_comp_koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n)).trans
    (RingedSite.koszulGeneratorsMap_eq_comp
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f n ℱ)

/-- **The last differential is killed by the projection onto
`ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`**, because it factors through the generator map. -/
theorem d_comp_koszulTopToQuotient (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).d ((r : ℤ) - 1) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ≫
        (koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n ≫ koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n) = 0 := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← koszulFromCoIdx_comp_koszulGenMap, Category.assoc,
    koszulGenMap_comp_cokernel_π_globalSpanMultiple, comp_zero]

/-- The canonical map from `ℱ` to the top cohomology sheaf of the Koszul complex: the inverse of
the top projection, followed by `HomologicalComplex.topToHomology`. -/
def koszulToTopHomology (n : ℕ) :
    ℱ ⟶ (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).homology ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) :=
  inv (koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n) ≫
    HomologicalComplex.topToHomology (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n) (next_top_eq_succ (r := r))
      (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ n)

/-- **The generator map is killed by the canonical map to the top cohomology sheaf**: it factors
through the last differential, which `HomologicalComplex.topToHomology` kills. -/
theorem koszulGenMap_comp_koszulToTopHomology (n : ℕ) :
    koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n ≫ koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n = 0 := by
  rw [koszulToTopHomology, ← koszulToCoIdx_comp_d_comp_koszulTopProjOn]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [IsIso.hom_inv_id_assoc, HomologicalComplex.d_comp_topToHomology, comp_zero]

/-- The subsheaf `(f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ` is killed by the canonical map to the top cohomology
sheaf: that map factors through the cokernel of the generator map, which the subsheaf is in the
kernel of. -/
theorem globalSpanMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule_koszulToTopHomology (n : ℕ) :
    globalSpanMultiple (koszulGlobalGenerator Y f) (n + 1) ℱ ≤
      kernelSubmodule (koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n) := by
  have hdesc : cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n) ≫
      cokernel.desc (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n) (koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n)
        (koszulGenMap_comp_koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n) = koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n :=
    cokernel.π_desc (C := Y.Modules) _ _ _
  refine le_trans (globalSpanMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule_koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n) ?_
  exact hdesc ▸ kernelSubmodule_le_kernelSubmodule_comp
    (cokernel.π (C := Y.Modules) (koszulGenMap Y f ℱ n)) _

/-- **The quotient `ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ` maps to the top cohomology sheaf.** -/
def quotientToKoszulTopHomology (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).obj (op n) ⟶
      (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).homology ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) := by
  refine cokernel.desc (C := Y.Modules) _ (koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n) ?_
  refine Scheme.Modules.hom_ext _ _ fun V => ?_
  ext y
  have hy := globalSpanMultiple_le_kernelSubmodule_koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n (op V) y.property
  rw [kernelSubmodule_toSubmodule_obj] at hy
  exact hy

/-- The quotient projection followed by `quotientToKoszulTopHomology` is the map
`koszulToTopHomology` from `ℱ` to the top cohomology sheaf. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem koszulQuotientπ_comp_quotientToKoszulTopHomology (n : ℕ) :
    koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n ≫ quotientToKoszulTopHomology Y f ℱ n =
      koszulToTopHomology Y f ℱ n :=
  cokernel.π_desc (C := Y.Modules) _ _ _

/-- **The top cohomology sheaf of the Koszul complex is the quotient
`ℱ / (f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})ℱ`**, as a map out of the cohomology sheaf. -/
def koszulTopHomologyToQuotient (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n).homology ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ⟶
      (koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).obj (op n) :=
  HomologicalComplex.descTopHomology (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n) (next_top_eq_succ (r := r))
    (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ n) ((r : ℤ) - 1) (prev_top_eq_pred (r := r))
    (koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n ≫ koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n)
    (d_comp_koszulTopToQuotient Y f ℱ n)

/-- The map from the top-degree term to the top cohomology sheaf, followed by
`koszulTopHomologyToQuotient`, is the top projection followed by the quotient projection. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem topToHomology_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient (n : ℕ) :
    HomologicalComplex.topToHomology (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n) (next_top_eq_succ (r := r))
          (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ n) ≫
        koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ n =
      koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ n ≫ koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n :=
  HomologicalComplex.topToHomology_comp_descTopHomology _ _ _ _ _ _ _

/-- **The comparison is an isomorphism.** -/
instance isIso_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient (n : ℕ) :
    IsIso (koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ n) := by
  refine ⟨quotientToKoszulTopHomology Y f ℱ n, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext_topToHomology _ (next_top_eq_succ (r := r))
      (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ n) ?_
    rw [Category.comp_id, topToHomology_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient_assoc,
      koszulQuotientπ_comp_quotientToKoszulTopHomology, koszulToTopHomology,
      IsIso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
  · refine (cancel_epi (koszulQuotientπ Y f ℱ n)).1 ?_
    rw [Category.comp_id, koszulQuotientπ_comp_quotientToKoszulTopHomology_assoc,
      koszulToTopHomology, Category.assoc, topToHomology_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient,
      IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

/-! ## The two towers, and the comparison between them -/

/-- **The dual Koszul tower with coefficients in `ℱ`, read in `Y.Modules`**: the inverse system
of the complexes `K(𝒪_Y, f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1}) ⊗ ℱ` whose transitions are the downward Koszul
transitions. This is the tower of the Koszul formula of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E], up to the shift by
`r` that `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulTensorDualSystemCoefficientIso` carries. -/
def koszulDualTowerOn : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ CochainComplex Y.Modules ℤ :=
  RingedSite.koszulDualSystemOn (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ

/-- The level `n` of the dual Koszul tower is the complex `koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n`. -/
@[simp]
theorem koszulDualTowerOn_obj (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulDualTowerOn Y f ℱ).obj (op n) = koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ n :=
  rfl

/-- The one-step transition of the dual Koszul tower, read in `Y.Modules`. -/
def koszulDualMapOn (m : ℕ) : koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ (m + 1) ⟶ koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ m :=
  RingedSite.koszulDualComplexOnMap (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ m

/-- The transition of the dual Koszul tower from level `m + 1` to level `m` is
`koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m`. -/
theorem koszulDualTowerOn_map_succ (m : ℕ) :
    (koszulDualTowerOn Y f ℱ).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_add_right m 1)).op =
      koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m :=
  RingedSite.koszulDualSystemOn_map_succ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ m

/-- **The transition of the dual Koszul tower is the identity on the top-degree factor.** The
factor is indexed by the full subset, whose complement is empty, so the monomial by which the
transition multiplies it is the empty one. -/
theorem koszulDualMapOn_f_top_comp_koszulTopProjOn (m : ℕ) :
    (koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m).f ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ≫ koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ m =
      koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ (m + 1) :=
  have hone : (RingedSite.koszulDualTransOn
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ m).app
      (AlternatingCech.topIdx r).1 = 𝟙 ℱ :=
    (RingedSite.koszulScalarOn_congr (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f
      (e' := 0) (fun i => by simp) ℱ).trans
        (RingedSite.koszulScalarOn_zero (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ)
  (AlternatingCech.mapX_comp_pi
      (RingedSite.koszulDualTransOn (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f ℱ m)
      (AlternatingCech.topIdx r)).trans
    ((congrArg (fun φ => koszulTopProjOn Y f ℱ (m + 1) ≫ φ) hone).trans (Category.comp_id _))

/-- **The comparison of the top cohomology sheaves with the quotient tower is a morphism of
towers.** -/
theorem homologyMap_koszulDualMapOn_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient (m : ℕ) :
    HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) ≫
        koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ m =
      koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ (m + 1) ≫
        (koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_add_right m 1)).op := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext_topToHomology _ (next_top_eq_succ (r := r))
    (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ (m + 1)) ?_
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← HomologicalComplex.topToHomology_naturality (koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m)
      (next_top_eq_succ (r := r)) (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ (m + 1))
      (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ m),
    Category.assoc, topToHomology_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient, ← Category.assoc,
    koszulDualMapOn_f_top_comp_koszulTopProjOn,
    topToHomology_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient_assoc, koszulQuotientπ_comp_map]

/-- The comparison of the dual Koszul tower with the quotient tower, at a single level. -/
def koszulTopSingleComparison (m : ℕ) :
    koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ m ⟶
      (HomologicalComplex.single Y.Modules (ComplexShape.up ℤ) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1)).obj
        ((koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).obj (op m)) :=
  HomologicalComplex.mkHomToSingle
    (HomologicalComplex.topToHomology (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ m) (next_top_eq_succ (r := r))
        (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ m) ≫
      koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ m)
    (fun i _ => HomologicalComplex.d_comp_topToHomology_comp (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ m)
      (next_top_eq_succ (r := r)) (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ m)
      (koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ m) i)

/-- **The comparison is an isomorphism on cohomology in the top degree, at every level.** This is
the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0G3D] at that degree, and it needs no refinement of the index. -/
instance isIso_homologyMap_koszulTopSingleComparison (m : ℕ) :
    IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ m)
      ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1)) :=
  HomologicalComplex.isIso_homologyMap_mkHomToSingle (koszulComplexOn Y f ℱ m)
    (next_top_eq_succ (r := r)) (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ m)
    (koszulTopHomologyToQuotient Y f ℱ m)

/-- **The comparison is compatible with the transitions of the two towers.** -/
theorem koszulTopSingleComparison_square (m : ℕ) :
    koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m ≫ koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ m =
      koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ (m + 1) ≫
        (HomologicalComplex.single Y.Modules (ComplexShape.up ℤ) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1)).map
          ((koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_add_right m 1)).op) := by
  rw [koszulTopSingleComparison, koszulTopSingleComparison,
    HomologicalComplex.mkHomToSingle_topToHomology_comp,
    HomologicalComplex.mkHomToSingle_topToHomology_comp, ← Category.assoc,
    HomologicalComplex.toSingleTopCohomology_naturality (koszulDualMapOn Y f ℱ m)
      (next_top_eq_succ (r := r)) (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ (m + 1))
      (koszulComplexOn_d_top_eq_zero Y f ℱ m),
    Category.assoc, Category.assoc, ← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp,
    homologyMap_koszulDualMapOn_comp_koszulTopHomologyToQuotient]

/-- **The comparison of the dual Koszul tower with the quotient tower placed in the top degree**,
as a morphism of towers of complexes. Its square is
`Stacks.Algebraization.koszulTopSingleComparison_square`. -/
def koszulDualToTopQuotient :
    koszulDualTowerOn Y f ℱ ⟶
      koszulTopQuotientSystem Y f ℱ ⋙
        HomologicalComplex.single Y.Modules (ComplexShape.up ℤ) ((r : ℤ) - 1 + 1) :=
  NatTrans.ofOpSequence (fun m => koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ m)
    (fun m => (congrArg (fun φ => φ ≫ koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ m)
      (koszulDualTowerOn_map_succ Y f ℱ m)).trans (koszulTopSingleComparison_square Y f ℱ m))

/-- The component of `koszulDualToTopQuotient` at level `m` is
`koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ m`. -/
theorem koszulDualToTopQuotient_app (m : ℕ) :
    (koszulDualToTopQuotient Y f ℱ).app (op m) = koszulTopSingleComparison Y f ℱ m :=
  rfl

end Scheme

end Stacks.Algebraization

